  "growth_comparison_note": "Construction is dominated by enumerating supported transitions, so the work ratio from four to five loci is nnz(5)/nnz(4) = 14.878. Measured construction time over that same step rose by 15.01 (dense), 15.09 (CSR) and 14.68 (hash), agreeing with the derived ratio to about 1.5 per cent. A least-squares exponent fitted over all of n = 1..5 instead gives 8.5 to 10.4, because fixed per-call overhead dominates the smallest problems and flattens the fitted slope. The asymptotic claim is therefore supported by the top of the measured range and not by the whole of it, which is what an asymptotic claim is entitled to.",
